@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Complex use case diagram — multi-channel banking with four actors and twelve-plus use cases across Teller, ATM, and Online subsystems, with include/extend/generalization.
'   usecase:      Teach multiple subsystem boundaries, cross-subsystem include/extend, and actor generalization at scale.
'   complexity:   complex
'   domain:       Banking
' ============================================================================
title Example Use Case Diagram - Complex Banking

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' Four actors:  Customer, Teller, FraudOfficer, SystemTimer.
' Three subsystems inside the Bank system boundary:
'   - Teller Channel
'   - ATM Channel
'   - Online Channel
' plus a shared core (Authenticate, Transfer, Statement).
' Relationships include «include» (Transfer includes Authenticate),
' «extend» (Overdraft Warning extends Transfer; SMS Alert extends Withdraw),
' actor generalization (Teller --|> Staff), and cross-boundary associations.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

left to right direction

actor "Customer"      as cust
actor "Teller"        as teller
actor "FraudOfficer"  as fraud
actor "SystemTimer"   as timer

' Actor generalization: Teller is specialised staff.
actor "Staff" as staff
teller --|> staff

rectangle "Bank" {

  ' ---- Shared core use cases ------------------------------------------
  usecase "Authenticate"      as ucAuth
  usecase "Transfer Funds"    as ucTransfer
  usecase "Request Statement" as ucStmt
  usecase "Review Fraud"      as ucFraud

  ' ---- Teller Channel -------------------------------------------------
  rectangle "Teller Channel" {
    usecase "Open Account"     as ucOpen
    usecase "Close Account"    as ucClose
    usecase "Cash Deposit"     as ucTDep
  }

  ' ---- ATM Channel ----------------------------------------------------
  rectangle "ATM Channel" {
    usecase "Withdraw Cash"     as ucWithdraw
    usecase "Check Balance"     as ucBal
    usecase "Print Mini-Stmt"   as ucMini
  }

  ' ---- Online Channel -------------------------------------------------
  rectangle "Online Channel" {
    usecase "Login"            as ucLogin
    usecase "Pay Bill"         as ucBill
    usecase "Set Up Alert"     as ucAlert
  }

  ' ---- Extensions (optional behaviour) --------------------------------
  usecase "Overdraft Warning" as ucOver
  usecase "SMS Notification"  as ucSms
}

' ===== Associations: actors -> use cases ================================
cust   --> ucAuth
cust   --> ucTransfer
cust   --> ucStmt
cust   --> ucWithdraw
cust   --> ucBal
cust   --> ucLogin
cust   --> ucBill
teller --> ucOpen
teller --> ucClose
teller --> ucTDep
fraud  --> ucFraud
timer  --> ucStmt       ' scheduled statements

' ===== «include» — mandatory invocation across subsystems ================
ucTransfer .> ucAuth    : <<include>>
ucLogin   .> ucAuth     : <<include>>
ucBill    .> ucTransfer : <<include>>
ucMini    .> ucStmt     : <<include>>

' ===== «extend» — optional, condition-gated ==============================
ucOver .> ucTransfer  : <<extend>>
ucSms  .> ucWithdraw  : <<extend>>
ucAlert .> ucSms       : <<extend>>

note right of ucOver
  <b>«extend» — Overdraft Warning</b>
  Condition: { transfer exceeds balance }.
  The base Transfer is valid without it;
  the warning adds behaviour only when
  triggered.
end note

note bottom of ucAuth
  <b>«include» — Authenticate</b>
  Transfer, Login, and (indirectly via
  Bill) other flows MUST authenticate.
  Factoring Authenticate out as an
  include keeps each base use case lean
  and centralises the security contract.
end note

note bottom of timer
  <b>Non-human actor</b>
  SystemTimer is an actor too — anything
  external that initiates behaviour counts,
  including schedulers and other systems.
end note

@enduml
